7592186045417 true] [17592186553810 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535994 17592186045417 true] [17592186553810 1083 #uuid "e2ae8cb1-1ad1-519a-a9ae-fc0f9b33b01f" 13194139535994 17592186045417 true] [17592186553811 1080 "3\\sqrt[3]{(x+2)^{4}}" 13194139535994 17592186045417 true] [17592186553811 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535994 17592186045417 true] [17592186553811 1083 #uuid "ec4a59e0-949a-5cc8-91d2-09ecb393925e" 13194139535994 17592186045417 true] [17592186553812 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553807 13194139535994 17592186045417 true] [17592186553812 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553808 13194139535994 17592186045417 true] [17592186553812 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553809 13194139535994 17592186045417 true] [17592186553812 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553810 13194139535994 17592186045417 true] [17592186553812 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553811 13194139535994 17592186045417 true] [17592186553812 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139535994 17592186045417 true] [17592186553812 1077 "selection" 13194139535994 17592186045417 true] [17592186553812 1078 #edb/ref 17592186553809 13194139535994 17592186045417 true] [17592186553812 1079 #uuid "8c497ffd-4cca-50b5-a7fc-dc93d720ea25" 13194139535994 17592186045417 true] [17592186553813 1068 #edb/ref 17592186553812 13194139535994 17592186045417 true] [17592186553813 1069 "q-138860" 13194139535994 17592186045417 true] [17592186553813 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535994 17592186045417 true] [17592186553813 1071 "Consider the function $y=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{({x}^{2}+2)^{6}}{3x+6}}.$ The derivative of this function is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{({x}^{2}+2)(11{x}^{2}+24x-2)}{g(x)}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $g(x).$" 13194139535994 17592186045417 true] [17592186553813 1072 #uuid "5c789989-28b9-52e0-ac72-a0f8b7d66a60" 13194139535994 17592186045417 true] [17592186553813 1074 "Our function can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{({x}^{2}+2)^{6}}{3x+6}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{({x}^{2}+2)^{6}}}{\\sqrt[3]{3x+6}} \\\\  & =\\frac{({x}^{2}+2)^{6/3}}{(3x+6)^{1/3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{({x}^{2}+2)^{2}}{(3x+6)^{1/3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we take the natural logarithm of both sides and use the quotient and power rules for logarithms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{({x}^{2}+2)^{2}}{(3x+6)^{1/3}}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(({x}^{2}+2)^{2})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡((3x+6)^{1/3}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+2)-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x+6)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+2)-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x+6)) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot {y}^{′} & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+2}\\cdot 2x-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3x+6}\\cdot 3 \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =\\frac{4x}{{x}^{2}+2}-\\frac{1}{3x+6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we solve for ${y}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =y(\\frac{4x}{{x}^{2}+2}-\\frac{1}{3x+6})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $y=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{({x}^{2}+2)^{6}}{3x+6}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{({x}^{2}+2)^{6}}{3x+6}}(\\frac{4x}{{x}^{2}+2}-\\frac{1}{3x+6}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{({x}^{2}+2)^{6}}{3x+6}}(\\frac{4x(3x+6)-({x}^{2}+2)}{({x}^{2}+2)(3x+6)}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{({x}^{2}+2)^{6}}{3x+6}}(\\frac{11{x}^{2}+24x-2}{({x}^{2}+2)(3x+6)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{({x}^{2}+2)(11{x}^{2}+24x-2)}{\\sqrt[3]{(3x-6)^{4}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\ng(x)=\\sqrt[3]{(3x-6)^{4}}.\n$$" 13194139535994 17592186045417 true] [17592186553814 1058 #edb/ref 17592186553815 13194139535994 17592186045417 true] [17592186553814 1062 #uuid "2ba10ec7-4252-52ba-8bc0-ceb77d7dadf1" 13194139535994 17592186045417 true] [17592186553814 1063 #edb/ref 17592186534067 13194139535994 17592186045417 true] [17592186553815 1058 #edb/ref 17592186553818 13194139535994 17592186045417 true] 